  # Vietnam: National AI Development Fund to Accelerate Innovation
  
  [Agentic AI](https://opengovasia.com/channel/agentic-ai/?c=us)•
  7 March, 2026
  
  ![Article Sam Viet Mar 07 2026 main](https://opengovasia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Article-Sam_Viet-Mar-07-2026-main.jpg)
  
  Vietnam is taking a significant step to [strengthen its artificial intelligence capabilities](https://en.vietnamplus.vn/vietnam-to-establish-national-ai-development-fund-post338685.vnp) with the establishment of a national AI development fund for the 2026–2027 period. The initiative, approved under Decision No. 367/QĐ‑TTg by the government, is part of the broader strategy to implement the recently passed Law on Artificial Intelligence.
  
  This fund is expected to play a pivotal role in accelerating AI research, innovation and practical applications across the country while also promoting responsible, ethical use of technology.
  
  The national AI development fund is designed as a dedicated financial mechanism to support the creation and deployment of AI solutions in both public and private sectors. It will mobilise resources to enhance Vietnam’s AI ecosystem, encourage innovation and foster collaboration between research institutions, technology companies, startups and government agencies.
  
  By providing targeted funding, the initiative aims to stimulate breakthroughs in AI technologies, support pilot projects and contribute to a digital transformation that strengthens the nation’s economic competitiveness.
  
  Under the implementation plan for the AI Law, the government will establish AI innovation clusters, linking physical hubs with digital networks across high-tech parks, research centres and technology zones.
  
  These clusters are intended to create a collaborative environment where enterprises, universities, research institutions and innovators can work together on AI development. They will also serve as platforms for testing, prototyping and commercialising AI solutions, promoting knowledge sharing and reducing barriers to adoption while encouraging entrepreneurship and startups to actively participate.
  
  The roadmap for implementing the AI Law assigns clear responsibilities to relevant ministries, agencies and local authorities to ensure coordinated enforcement. It emphasises synchronised action, defined timelines and accountability measures, aiming to raise awareness of AI regulations and encourage compliance among officials, businesses and the general public.
  
  This structured approach is expected to facilitate the safe, ethical and effective use of AI technologies in line with national priorities, fostering trust and public confidence in AI applications.
  
  In addition to funding and cluster development, the implementation plan outlines the drafting of decrees and guidelines to support the AI Law. These measures will define standards for high-risk AI systems, establish a national AI ethics framework and provide guidance on the collection and use of datasets essential for AI development.
  
  By setting clear regulations and ethical standards, the government seeks to balance innovation with responsible AI deployment, ensuring that technology benefits both society and the economy.
  
  The plan also highlights the importance of human capital development and infrastructure enhancement. Ministries are tasked with integrating AI objectives into sectoral plans, ensuring resources are allocated for AI research and facilitating training programs to develop a skilled AI workforce.
  
  Advanced infrastructure, such as a national AI database, one-stop electronic portals and research support centres, will be established to support data accessibility and streamline AI-related processes.
  
  Vietnam’s push to establish a national AI development fund underscores its commitment to becoming a leading player in the regional AI landscape. By supporting innovation, creating a collaborative ecosystem and ensuring regulatory compliance, the initiative aims to enhance the nation’s digital economy.
  
  It also seeks to position Vietnam as a competitive hub for AI research, development and application. This comprehensive approach reflects the government’s recognition of AI as a strategic driver for future growth, societal development and sustainable economic transformation.
  
  The fund will act as a cornerstone for Vietnam’s AI strategy, encouraging both domestic and international investment, promoting technological self-reliance and ensuring that AI adoption contributes to economic advancement, improved public services and enhanced quality of life for citizens.
  
  By combining funding, regulation, infrastructure, human capital development and strong collaboration, Vietnam is laying the foundation for a sustainable, innovative and technology-driven future that embraces both progress and responsibility.
  
